# Lanebreakers — Project Overview

## What this is

**Lanebreakers** is a browser mid-lane MOBA: short matches, creep waves, fountain bases, one tower per side, 14 heroes, item shop, classic bot + neural AI, practice / online / tournament / TRAIN.

This repo is the **canonical game codebase** — Vite + TypeScript modules, not a single HTML file. Player-facing features, balance, and sim rules all live here.

Human docs: `README.md` (day-to-day guide for humans and agents).

## Stack

- **Vite + TypeScript**, Canvas 2D, light DOM for menus/shop (no React/Angular)
- Ship targets: `npm run build:pages` → `dist/` (GitHub Pages); `npm run build:release` → single HTML in `dist-release/`; `npm run desktop:dist` → Electron packages in `dist-desktop/` (itch / Steam — see `DESKTOP.md`)
- Prefer plain modules; keep **`src/sim/` free of `document` / canvas** so browser and Node trainer share one ruleset
- Electron is a **thin shell** (`electron/`) over the same Vite build — do not fork a second game for desktop stores

## Layout (where to edit)

```
src/
  data/     world constants, heroes, items
  sim/      headless match rules (newSim, simStep, combat, abilities, …)
  ai/       classic bot + neural/ (runtime, train UI, baked brains)
  app/      match shell, netplay, lobby, tournament, persistence, boot
  render/   canvas world / HUD / FX
  ui/       DOM shop, menus, books, input, end card
  styles/   CSS (game.css imports base / menus / shop / overlay)
  headless.ts / node-sim.ts   Node trainer bundle entry
```

| Want to change… | Look in… |
|-----------------|----------|
| Stats, economy, win conditions | `src/data/` |
| Combat, abilities, waves, shop timing | `src/sim/` |
| Bots / TRAIN / brains | `src/ai/` |
| Lobby, online, tournament, match start | `src/app/` |
| Drawing / HUD | `src/render/` |
| Menus / shop panel / CSS | `src/ui/`, `src/styles/` |

Import sim via `src/sim` or `src/sim/engine`. Neural code talks to the sim through a small API object (cast, buy, armor, …) — same idea as the old `LB_API`.

## How the match runs

- Practice / host: run `simStep` locally; apply player/bot commands with `applyCmd`
- Online clients: interpolate `buildSnapshot` packets (`SNAP_HZ`); host is authoritative
- Client session state lives in `G` (`src/app/state.ts`) — mode, lobby, camera, FX buffers, etc.

## Commands agents should know

```bash
npm install
npm run dev              # local play / iterate
npm run build            # typecheck + dist/ (Github Pages)
npm run build:release    # single-file HTML
npm run build:sim        # REQUIRED before Node training after sim/data changes
npm run bake:brains      # refresh src/ai/neural/brains/baked.json from trainer output
npm run smoke            # headless sim sanity
npm run smoke:neural
npm run smoke:parity
```

Never hand-edit `dist-sim/` — always regenerate with `npm run build:sim`.

## AI trainer (`ai/` in this repo)

Node training scripts live under **`ai/`**. They load **`dist-sim/index.cjs`** via `ai/engine.js` (modular only — no HTML scrape).

After changing `src/sim/` or sim-facing `src/data/`:

1. `npm run build:sim`
2. Train from `ai/` (`train.js` / `versus.js` / `lab.js` / `panel.js`)
3. `npm run bake:brains` (or enable bake in the Actions workflow)

Override sim path with `LB_SIM` if needed. See `README.md` and `ai/README.md`.

### GitHub Actions

`.github/workflows/train-ai.yml` runs background training on GitHub:

- `npm ci` → `npm run build:sim` → verify `loadGame()` → `ai/supervise.js`
- Caches / artifacts `ai/brains/<recipe>`; optional commit + bake

Do not remove the `build:sim` step — training will fail without `dist-sim`.

## How to enable GitHub Pages

The game is already Pages-ready. Agents wiring this up should:

1. **Build:** `npm ci && npm run build:pages` (alias of `npm run build`).
2. **Publish the `dist/` folder** (not repo root, not `dist-release/`).
3. **Base path:** `vite.config.ts` sets `base: './'` so asset URLs work from a project site (`https://user.github.io/repo/`) or a custom domain.

### Repo settings (manual)

GitHub → Settings → Pages → Source: **GitHub Actions** (preferred) or Deploy from a branch/`docs` folder if they insist on a static branch.

### Suggested workflow (agents may add `.github/workflows/pages.yml`)

```yaml
name: Deploy GitHub Pages
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  workflow_dispatch:
permissions:
  contents: read
  pages: write
  id-token: write
concurrency:
  group: pages
  cancel-in-progress: true
jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with: { node-version: '22', cache: npm }
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npm run build:pages
      - uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3
        with: { path: dist }
  deploy:
    needs: build
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    environment: { name: github-pages, url: ${{ steps.dep.outputs.page_url }} }
    steps:
      - id: dep
        uses: actions/deploy-pages@v4
```

Do **not** confuse this with `build:release` (single self-contained HTML for Releases downloads) or `build:sim` (Node trainer bundle).

## AI in this repo

- **Classic** — `src/ai/bot.ts` (`botThink`)
- **Neural** — `src/ai/neural/` (brains JSON `format: lanebreaker-brain-2`; bump format only when inputs change, then retrain)
- **Train UI** — in-browser genetic trainer in `ai/neural/train.ts`
- Tiers Rookie → Brutal (+ optional schools); Classic falls back to `botThink`

## Design principles (go-forward)

1. **One ruleset.** Game and trainer share `src/sim/` — never duplicate combat math for the bot or Node.
2. **Headless sim.** `newSim` / `simStep` must run without a browser (`npm run smoke`, `dist-sim`).
3. **Right layer.** Data in `data/`, rules in `sim/`, presentation in `render`/`ui`, modes/net in `app/`.
4. **Ship all targets.** Keep Pages (`dist/`), single-file (`dist-release/`), and desktop (`dist-desktop/` via Electron) working. Steam later reuses the desktop pack — see `DESKTOP.md`.
5. **Scoped changes.** No drive-by refactors; don't expand scope beyond the request.
6. **Optional cleanup** (when asked): split `abilities.ts` per hero, drop `@ts-nocheck`, tighten types — not required for play.

## Working agreements for agents

- Follow `README.md` for workflows
- After sim / AI / shared API changes, run `npm run smoke` (and `build` / `build:sim` when relevant)
- Do not reintroduce HTML scraping or a second parallel ruleset for training
- Keep new files modular; avoid collapsing the game back into one mega-file
- Recipes live only in `ai/recipes.json` (browser TRAIN imports that file — do not recreate a duplicate under `src/`)
